# Codex Automation runner profile

Use this profile when bootstrap runs inside the Codex app and the user chooses
Codex as the runner surface. Create three recurring project automations, one per
role, against `{{repo_path}}`.

Recommended cadence:

```text
implementer: every {{implementer_interval}}
reviewer: every {{reviewer_interval}}
fixer: every {{fixer_interval}}
```

Automation prompt for each role:

```text
Load the autonomous-work-loops skill and run exactly one {{role}} tick in {{repo_path}}.

Use the guarded Codex runner if it exists:

{{repo_path}}/.agent-loops/runners/codex.sh "{{repo_path}}" {{role}}

Reconstruct all state from GitHub and .agent-loops/ before acting. Do one unit of
work and exit. Do not install cron jobs. Do not create additional scheduled
automations. If no work is eligible, no-op and report that state.
```

Use project/worktree automation when isolation from the user's active checkout is
more important than direct local edits. Use local project automation only when
the user accepts that scheduled runs can mutate the current checkout.
